# Reference Point — Phone Sheet Dim (`.hybrid-chat-demo-dim`)

When the user says **"reference point"** or **"copy this design"** for a phone modal dim/scrim (dark overlay behind a bottom sheet), match `.hybrid-chat-demo-dim` in `#ai-layer` → `.hybrid-chat-demo-phone`.

## Structure

```html
<div class="hybrid-chat-demo-phone">
  <!-- nav, hero, product UI behind -->
  <div class="hybrid-chat-demo-dim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="hybrid-chat-demo-sheet">
    <!-- bottom sheet content -->
  </div>
</div>
```

Dim sits **under** the sheet (`z-index: 2`), sheet at `z-index: 3`. Both are `position: absolute` inside the phone.

## Visual spec

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Element | `.hybrid-chat-demo-dim` |
| Position | `absolute; inset: 0` |
| Background | **`rgba(26, 21, 15, 0.32)`** — warm ink, 32% opacity |
| Z-index | **2** (sheet above at 3+) |
| Interaction | Decorative: `aria-hidden="true"` (non-button). Clickable scrims use `<button>` with same fill. |

## CSS

```css
.hybrid-chat-demo-dim {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background: rgba(26, 21, 15, 0.32);
  z-index: 2;
}
```

## Apply to other phone overlays

Use the same fill on:

- `.var-d .cert-sheet-scrim`
- `.var-d .cert-chat-scrim`
- `.to-feature .to-tradeoff-scrim`

(Those may also animate `opacity: 0 → 1` when open — keep transitions; only match the **background** color.)

## Do not

- Use cool/neutral black (`rgba(0,0,0,…)`) — stay warm `26, 21, 15`.
- Drop opacity below ~0.28 or above ~0.4 — product hero must stay readable but clearly recessed.
- Place dim above the sheet — sheet must paint on top.
